    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package to satisfy all acceptance criteria. Key changes:\n\n1. **varint.py**: Fixed `decode_uvarint` to properly handle multi-byte LEB128 encoding (was only reading single byte).\n\n2. **header.py**: Changed record count from big-endian to little-endian (`struct.pack(\"<I\", count)` instead of `\">I\"`), matching the actual sample files.\n\n3. **crc.py**: Added final XOR (`^ 0xFFFFFFFF`) to `compute_crc` to produce standard CRC-32 values matching the samples. Also changed `unpack_crc` to raise `WFormatError(\"truncated\")` instead of `ValueError`.\n\n4. **codec.py**: Added alignment padding (ALIGN=4) to both `encode_record` and `decode_record` — each record's raw bytes (tag varint + length varint + payload) are padded to a multiple of 4 bytes. Added CRC verification in `unpack()`. All errors now raise `WFormatError` with appropriate `kind`.\n\n5. **stream.py**: Completely rewrote `iter_records` to be truly streaming using a `_StreamBuffer` class that only uses fixed-size `read(n)` calls",
